  "root": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "pankaj.kumar@stryker.com",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Aug 23 2019 18:13:48 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/responsivegrid",
    "text": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Mon Feb 15 2021 16:25:45 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p>Dr. Homer Stryker, an orthopaedic surgeon, established The Orthopedic Frame company 80 years ago, and the company eventually became Stryker, a global leader in medical technology. Dr. Stryker dedicated his life to serving patients, and his inspirational words, “If your tools don’t work, make them work,” continue to inspire and push us forward on behalf of the physicians and healthcare providers we serve. Our extensive portfolio of products and services help healthcare professionals specializing in Orthopaedics, MedSurg, Neurotechnology and Spine improve and save lives. We have a strong global presence and have grown to over 40,000 employees worldwide.</p>\n<p>The company’s 80<sup>th</sup> anniversary is a time of reflection and appreciation for what came before. As we explore the humble beginnings of Stryker, we find the thread that sutures together past and present: A surgeon, an inventor, a man driven to make healthcare better.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><b>Humble beginnings</b><br>\nWhen local community members recently found a set of vintage crutches, etched with the name “Dr. Stryker,” it was clear that they were a product of our founder’s innovative spirit and “almost legendary”<sup>1</sup> service to his community.</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Thu Feb 18 2021 21:42:30 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
