    },
    "text_45094066": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "jcr:createdBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
      "jcr:created": "Mon Feb 15 2021 16:28:47 GMT+0000",
      "text": "<p>The crutches, discovered at a garage sale, are likely examples of his pioneering surgical work in leg-length discrepancies.<sup>1</sup> Dr. Stryker, who first arrived in Kalamazoo, Michigan as a general practitioner, was appointed to serve as the physician for Kalamazoo County, treating community members in need and later becoming an orthopaedic surgeon.</p>\n<p>Building on his desire to meet the needs of surgeons by developing technology to advance healthcare, it was at this time that Dr. Stryker began the journey that established Stryker as a leading medical technology company. With early inventions such as the turning frame, walking heel and later, the oscillating saw.</p>\n<p>Today, though our portfolio of products and services has grown, our culture still reflects our founder's legacy and is underpinned by our mission and values. Of the process of building our <a href=\"https://www.stryker.com/us/en/about.html\">mission and values</a>, Chair and CEO, Kevin Lobo, says, “We knew we got it right based on the reaction of employees across the company as well as past leaders like our Chairman Emeritus, John Brown, who universally said, ‘this feels like us.’”</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
      "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Feb 19 2021 21:49:17 GMT+0000",
      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true",
      "cq:responsive": {
